## Lore

The infantryman of the New German Republic, taught combat, basic radio, tank piloting and self defence. One of the few NGR military O.C.C.s given no power armour or robot training, though the soldier may crew a robot vehicle or serve as pilot or gunner in a tank, APC or hover vehicle.

Half of the active infantry are human refugees from outside the NGR. Most become career soldiers.

Alignment: Any.

## Rank and pay

Standard military, private to lieutenant colonel. Salary is 1000 credits a month, rising to 3000 for ninth level and higher, with quarters, food, clothing and medical care provided. Quarters are dormitory style, four soldiers to an area, each with a private bedroom and shared living space; the soldier may live off base at his own expense.

## Cybernetics

None to start. Basic cyber-implants may be purchased or awarded for acts of heroism.

## GM Notes

A soldier may be serving or retired. An ex-soldier keeps the O.C.C. and its skills and works freelance, buying his own weapons, armour and equipment; the cost is experience, needing 25% more points for every subsequent level. An active soldier answers to military authority and may be court-martialled, imprisoned or dishonourably discharged.

Equipment available upon assignment includes additional weapons, a portable language translator, T-11 Enhanced body armour, the T-100 Eagle jet pack, an APC, the XM-200 mini-tank and access to tanks and other vehicles, plus low-security access to most military bases and to military doctors and hospitals. Availability depends on the local commander, supply, location, casualties and combat conditions, and the combat soldier is typically last on the priority list.
', 'published', 'data-script'
